From t.jombart at imperial.ac.uk  Fri Aug 24 14:54:35 2012
From: t.jombart at imperial.ac.uk (Jombart, Thibaut)
Date: Fri, 24 Aug 2012 12:54:35 +0000
Subject: [adegenet-forum] pop argument
In-Reply-To: <39B81D36-5B74-43C5-80C8-0C0FE01AA781@gmail.com>
References: <39B81D36-5B74-43C5-80C8-0C0FE01AA781@gmail.com>
Message-ID: <2CB2DA8E426F3541AB1907F98ABA6570579DD400@icexch-m1.ic.ac.uk>

Hello, 

you need to use 'pop(x) <- ...' to change or set population information; for instance, using simulated data:

> x <- glSim(10,100)
> pop(x)
 [1] A A A A A B B B B B
Levels: A B
> pop(x) <- rep(1:2, c(2,8))
> pop(x)
 [1] 1 1 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2
Levels: 1 2

Cheers

Thibaut


